sequenceDiagram
  title: Bridge Communication Flow - Lua and JavaScript

  participant LUA as Lua Runtime
  participant BRIDGE as Bridge C++
  participant TRANSPORT as WebviewTransport
  participant JS as JavaScript

  @start_note right of LUA
    Lua to JavaScript Flow
  @end_note

  LUA ->> BRIDGE : ctx:emit({name:"update", data:"test"})
  BRIDGE ->> BRIDGE : Serialize to JSON
  BRIDGE ->> TRANSPORT : Send RPC message
  
  TRANSPORT ->> JS : webview_eval("__coconut_dispatch_event(...)")
  JS ->> JS : Parse JSON
  JS ->> JS : Dispatch to listeners
  
  @start_note right of JS
    JavaScript to Lua Flow
  @end_note

  JS ->> TRANSPORT : coconut.call("command", payload)
  TRANSPORT ->> BRIDGE : webview_bind callback
  BRIDGE ->> BRIDGE : Parse RPC envelope
  
  alt call type
    BRIDGE ->> LUA : Dispatch to command handler
    LUA ->> LUA : Execute command
    LUA ->> BRIDGE : Return result
    BRIDGE ->> TRANSPORT : Send kReturn
    TRANSPORT ->> JS : Resolve Promise
  else event type
    BRIDGE ->> LUA : Dispatch event
    LUA ->> LUA : Execute event handlers
  end

  @start_note right of LUA
    Error Flow
  @end_note

  LUA ->> BRIDGE : Command throws error
  BRIDGE ->> TRANSPORT : Send kError
  TRANSPORT ->> JS : Reject Promise
  
  @start_note right of JS
    catch(err) handles error
  @end_note
